# Ignore large AI models
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# Bytecode Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Signing secret and demo database: regenerated on first start. The root
# .jwt_secret had always been ignored, the one in demo/ had escaped the
# rule — and the repository became public (point 66).
demo/.jwt_secret
demo/app.db

# Artifacts of the generalized offensive audit (tests/test_exploit_all.py):
# each example is compiled then served FROM THE ROOT of the repository, which
# drops the generated application and its throwaway database there. Ignoring
# them at the root avoids committing a secret by mistake (app.py +
# .jwt_secret).
#
# The patterns are ANCHORED, and it is not zeal. Without a leading slash,
# `app.py` means "at any depth": the rule caught src/monl_platform/app.py, and
# the module carrying the WHOLE web platform — routes, download, HTTP MCP
# endpoint — vanished from the repository without a word. A fresh clone could
# no longer start `monl-platform`, and tests/test_platform_web.py failed at
# collection in CI. The same defect had already cost six tests with
# `projets/` (point 116). A compilation artifact is only born in TWO places of
# the repository: the root (offensive audit) and demo/ (`monl compile
# demo/spec.ml`, docs/DEMO.md); everywhere else — build/, dist/, projets/,
# platform-projects/ — the whole folder is ignored, further down.
/app.py
/schema.sql
/app.db
/.monl_uploads/
/manage.py
/sandbox_ai.py
/.jwt_secret
demo/app.py
demo/schema.sql
demo/manage.py
demo/sandbox_ai.py
demo/.monl_uploads/

# Locally compiled projects. Everything 'monl' produces lives in projets/ —
# a single folder to ignore rather than one line per application, and the
# repository root stops filling with applications in the middle of the
# compiler's code. (demo/ is the reference demo, tracked on purpose:
# test_demo.py relies on it. Only its INPUTS are versioned — spec.ml,
# frontend/, assets/ — never app.db or .jwt_secret, ignored above. projets/
# stays the local sandbox: pouring six .jwt_secret into a public repository
# would reopen point 66.)
/projets/

# Rapport de couverture (point 63)
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Visual variation seed: the comment in generator/theme.py had always
# claimed it was ignored — it was not.
.monl_theme_seed

# Local measurements of AI calls: tokens/duration, never prompts or keys.
.monl_ai_usage.jsonl

# Package build artifacts (point 65) and local beta archives
*.egg-info/
archives/
# dist/ is the output of `python -m build`, attached to releases but never
# versioned; build/ serves setuptools AND the output folder the quick start
# suggests (`--output build/...`) — two artifacts, neither written by hand.
/dist/
/build/

# Local state of the web platform: accounts, projects and compiled
# artifacts. This data must never enter the compiler's history.
/platform.db
/platform-projects/

# Local deployment settings: the versioned example stays shareable; the
# real values (URL, OAuth, secrets) must never enter Git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.platform.example
